BT /F1 10 Tf 50 720 Td (IN THE MADRAS HIGH COURT \(MADURAI BENCH\)
CASE NO: Crl.O.P.\(MD\) No. 5120 of 2026
CNR NUMBER: HCMD010789122026
YEAR: 2026

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Justice K.K. Ramakrishnan

PARTIES:
P. Chelladurai
... Petitioner\(s\) / Appellant\(s\)
Versus
State represented by Inspector of Police, Alangulam Police Station, Tenkasi District
... Respondent\(s\)

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Mines and Minerals \(Development and Regulation\) Act 1957, Code of Criminal Procedure 1973

SECTIONS & PROVISIONS:
MMDR Act Section 21, CrPC Section 451, BNSS Section 497

KEY TOPICS & ISSUES:
Illegal Sand Mining, Vehicle Seizure, Interim Custody, Section 451 CrPC, District Mineral Foundation

================================================================================
                                   JUDGMENT
================================================================================

1. FACTS OF THE CASE:
Vehicle seized for transporting river sand without valid e-transit pass. Magistrate dismissed interim custody petition.

2. ISSUES FRAMED:
Should commercial vehicles seized in mineral offenses be kept idle in police stations causing natural decay?

3. LEGAL RATIO & FINDINGS:
Seized commercial vehicles should not be allowed to rust at police stations; conditional interim custody must be granted under Sunderbhai Ambalal Desai.

4. FINAL ORDER:
Interim Custody Granted with conditions; Tipper lorry released subject to deposit of Rs. 1 Lakh before mineral foundation.

Ordered and decreed accordingly.

Hon'ble Justice K.K. Ramakrishnan
Madras High Court \(Madurai Bench\)
[LEXGUARD REPOSITORY CRYPTOGRAPHIC SEAL]
) Tj ET
